.TH SYS_VM_SWAP 2 "2026-05-09" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_swap \- query swap device statistics
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_swap(sys_swapinfo_t *" swap ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_swap ()
enumerates configured swap backing stores.  Each entry is a
.B sys_swapinfo_t :
.PP
.RS
.nf
typedef struct sys_swapinfo {
    char     path[256];
    uint64_t total;       /* bytes */
    uint64_t used;        /* bytes */
    int      priority;
} sys_swapinfo_t;
.fi
.RE
.PP
On entry
.I *count
is the array capacity; on return it is the actual number of swap
devices.  Substrate currently exposes a single aggregate swap pool
via
.BR vm_swap_get_stats ;
when configured the syscall returns one synthetic entry named
.B swap0
with
.B priority
= 0.  Per-device enumeration becomes available once the swap
subsystem grows a public iterator.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; on failure -1 and
.I errno
is set per the error contract.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I swap
or
.I count
is NULL.
.TP
.B EFAULT
either pointer is unmapped.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_info (2),
.BR sys_vm_slabs (2)
